_input":{"command":"for d in DocService/sources DocService . .. ../.. ../../.. /; do ls -d \"$d/node_modules/mongodb\" 2>/dev/null || echo \"absent: $d/node_modules/mongodb\"; done; echo \"NODE_PATH=${NODE_PATH:-unset}\"; ls DocService/sources/config.json 2>&1; git ls-files | grep -c \"config.json$\"; git ls-files | grep \"sources/config.json\"; grep -n -A25 \"ignores\" eslint.config.js | head -30","description":"Check mongodb in each Node resolution directory and config.json"}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_01WP93F1gBaDnxyRF9jnVW5U","tool_input":{"command":"ls -d DocService/sources/node_modules/mongodb DocService/node_modules/mongodb node_modules/mongodb ../node_modules/mongodb ../../node_modules/mongodb ../../../node_modules/mongodb /node_modules/mongodb /usr/lib/node_modules/mongodb /usr/local/lib/node_modules/mongodb; ls DocService/sources/config.json; git ls-files | grep \"sources/config.json\"; printenv NODE_PATH; grep -n -A25 \"ignores\" eslint.config.js | head -30","description":"Check mongodb in each resolution directory and config.json"}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_01FJYam7brwwQqSwoucgkFBR","tool_input":{"command":"sed -n 60,96p Gruntfile.js; git ls-files | grep -i \"build.*\\.json$\\|grunt\" | head","description":"Check what the Gruntfile copies"}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_01WzC3sXZaqm7gA1ATncAn6m","tool_input":{"command":"theseus validate; git diff --stat; git diff --numstat","description":"Validate Theseus state and check diff size"}}],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"safety_stops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":32,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"`DocService/sources/database.js` is dead code: nothing uses it and it cannot load. I recorded the finding in `.theseus/atlas/docservice.md` and committed it as `82ac6d5`. No source code was changed. The packet has no acceptance commands, so there was nothing to run; the change is one file and 27 lines, within budget.\n\n**`database.js`**\n- **Nothing calls it.** I searched the whole repo outside `node_modules`: sources, tests, `Gruntfile.js`, `Makefile`, the Dockerfile, the GitHub workflows and every `package.json`. Every hit for \"database\" is the separate `databaseConnectors/` folder or a Theseus document.\n- **Nothing loads it by a built name either.** The only places that build a module path at runtime are the editor-data storage setting (`DocsCoServer.js:100-101`, `changes2forgotten.js:42`, `notificationService.js:36`) and `moduleReloader`, which only loads npm packages. Neither can reach `database.js`.\n- **It isn't packaged.** It's not a `bin` entry and not in any `pkg.scripts` list, so it isn't bundled into the `docservice` binary.\n- **It cannot load.** Its `mongodb` dependency is in no `package.json` or lockfile and isn't installed anywhere in the worktree. The `./config.json` it reads doesn't exist either. It also uses an old MongoDB driver API that was dropped in driver 3.0.\n\nI could not run the actual load test, because this run wasn't allowed to execute `node`. That proof is from the code only. A reviewer can confirm it with `cd DocService/sources && node -e \"require('./database.js')\"`, which should fail with `MODULE_NOT_FOUND` for `mongodb`.\n\n**`editorDataRedis.js`**\nIt is listed in three `pkg.scripts` lists (DocService, FileConverter and AdminPanel), but the file doesn't exist in this repo. It's a stale packaging entry, and only `editorDataMemory` can run here. It was most likely inherited from the upstream server, where a Redis backend is shipped as a separate add-on (the `Gruntfile` has a `--addon` mechanism for that). I can't prove this: the git history starts at a single import commit. `pkg` should simply skip a missing file without failing the build, but I didn't run a build to check.\n\n**Not done because this run forbade it**\n- **Follow-up packets not created.** Writing under `.theseus/queue/` wasn't allowed, so I couldn't run `theseus packet new`. The four proposed packets are listed in the card under \"Proposed packets (not created)\": delete `database.js`, and remove `editorDataRedis.js` from each of the three `pkg.scripts` lists. Before the last three, check that no deployment of this fork supplies its own `editorDataRedis.js` at build time.\n- **Friction not recorded.** `.theseus/scoreboard/friction.jsonl` is outside the packet's target, so I didn't append to it. The friction to record: the queue restriction blocks the spawned-packet step this packet asks for, as it did for PKT-0009, and running `node` and `theseus validate` was not approved.\n\n**Lessons for the Atlas** (already in the card)\n- A \"no callers\" check has to cover module paths built at runtime and the packaging lists (`bin`, `pkg.scripts`), not only plain `require('./x')` lines.\n- Dead code here shows three independent signs: no caller of either kind, no packaging entry, and a dependency missing from every lockfile.\n- I also answered the card's open question about which editor-data backends exist: in this repo, only `editorDataMemory`.","ttft_ms":2193,"type":"result","duration_ms":126074,"uuid":"8d4d526b-8e2d-4313-9577-7d8f1171b712","ttft_stream_ms":947,"time_to_request_ms":382,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":6,"system_prompt":199,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":4,"input_attachments":19,"input_hooks":2,"conversation_append":1,"transcript_persist":6,"tool_pool_refresh":1,"init_message":6,"init_frame_send":9,"engine_pickup":10,"loop_entry":6,"message_prep":2,"model_config_wait":1,"autocompact":3,"request_announcements":15,"query_setup":5,"auto_mode_context_wait":31,"model_gates":0,"tool_schema_build":